      "text": "Ensure that every single cell inside the Excel output that the Excel export Python script creates is dynamic, it is not fixed. And I want you to have default values 0. I do not want hardcoded values anywhere in the Excel file so I can get fresh values every single time, and if the script fails to produce a\ncertain value for certain columns, then leave that column empty so we can know where the script is lacking. \nI want you to add a year-on-year percentage gain column into the PNL metrics sheet along with the total PNL of each year. Add the percentage gain column beside it and calculate it for monthly as well. And I want this percentage calculated based on the starting equity for that particular month or any\ntime period. Do not take the starting equity of 10 lakh as a base price to calculate the PNL percentage. \nI want the index comparison sheet inside the excel output to be populated for all the indices currently only as the strategy data, but I also want the indices data. And for this, I want to store the indices data somewhere so the script don't have to actually calculate the same data again and again for\nindices.\nI want the average candles held column inside the PNL metrics sheet to be populated correctly. And I also want a starting capital for each period in the PNL metrics sheet. \nIn the summary sheet in the Excel file, Move Risk-Free Benchmark Rate, Sharpe Ratio, Sortino Ratio, Calmar Ratio, Profit Factor, SQN, Kelly Criterion, Expectancy per Trade, Percentage per Trade below the Setup and Strategy Rules. At the end, I want the CAGR, Total Net PNL, Drawdown, Winning\nTrades, Winning Ratio, and Accuracy to be at the top, just after the Setup and Strategy Rules. \nIn the Idle Cash sheet, the Date column is not following my proper Excel formatting. Look at the other columns in that sheet only and copy the formatting of column B into column A in the Date column in the Idle Cash sheet. \nIn the computational annual sheet, I want a clear segregation between the tax levied on the equity PNL and the tax levied on the liquid PNL. Currently, I am unable to understand exactly how much my equity portfolio is getting taxed. And what does the column Tax Equity STCG 20 8% mean, and Tax\nEquity LTCG 13 0% mean? \nLiquid Fund Trades sheet, columns A, B, C, E, F are not following our proper formatting. Update them. \nIn the entire Excel file, except the trades sheet, everywhere the date is written, it is not following our formatting, background color, text color, and those kinds of formatting. Update the date column and date and time column. \nIn the rolling returns summary sheet, I cannot compare the strategy returns with the Nifty rolling returns properly. In this rolling returns summary, I want all of the rolling periods: 3 months, 6 months, 1 year, 2 years, 3 years, 5 years, 7 years, 7.5 years, and 10 years rolling return of the strategy and of\nthe indices. And I want all the indices. \nCurrently, we have three sheets for rolling returns. I only want one sheet, as I mentioned above. \nAnd I want the exposure sheet correctly calculated and filled with the correct data. There is a column in the trades sheet called ENTRY_ATR_14. Remove that. Remove ATR 14 mention from all of the scripts, be it daily or weekly. In the trades sheet, the vwap_tight and the weekly_vwap_tight columns\nare not being filled. The entry_cumulative_rsi_2_2, entry_rsi_2, entry_intraday_intensity_21, weekly_intraday_intensity, mfi_10, and entry_daily_average_dollar_volume_200 all of these columns are not being filled correctly. Update the excel file to fill it correctly. And remove the columns from AQ to AT\nwhich contain the other indices, we do not need them. And move the entry_reason and exit_reason column after the candles_held column. And also move the stop_price column after the candle_held column. ",
      "fontSize": 4.1715274778054034,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Ensure that every single cell inside the Excel output that the Excel export Python script creates is dynamic, it is not fixed. And I want you to have default values 0. I do not want hardcoded values anywhere in the Excel file so I can get fresh values every single time, and if the script fails to produce a certain value for certain columns, then leave that column empty so we can know where the script is lacking. \nI want you to add a year-on-year percentage gain column into the PNL metrics sheet along with the total PNL of each year. Add the percentage gain column beside it and calculate it for monthly as well. And I want this percentage calculated based on the starting equity for that particular month or any time period. Do not take the starting equity of 10 lakh as a base price to calculate the PNL percentage. \nI want the index comparison sheet inside the excel output to be populated for all the indices currently only as the strategy data, but I also want the indices data. And for this, I want to store the indices data somewhere so the script don't have to actually calculate the same data again and again for indices.\nI want the average candles held column inside the PNL metrics sheet to be populated correctly. And I also want a starting capital for each period in the PNL metrics sheet. \nIn the summary sheet in the Excel file, Move Risk-Free Benchmark Rate, Sharpe Ratio, Sortino Ratio, Calmar Ratio, Profit Factor, SQN, Kelly Criterion, Expectancy per Trade, Percentage per Trade below the Setup and Strategy Rules. At the end, I want the CAGR, Total Net PNL, Drawdown, Winning Trades, Winning Ratio, and Accuracy to be at the top, just after the Setup and Strategy Rules. \nIn the Idle Cash sheet, the Date column is not following my proper Excel formatting. Look at the other columns in that sheet only and copy the formatting of column B into column A in the Date column in the Idle Cash sheet. \nIn the computational annual sheet, I want a clear segregation between the tax levied on the equity PNL and the tax levied on the liquid PNL. Currently, I am unable to understand exactly how much my equity portfolio is getting taxed. And what does the column Tax Equity STCG 20 8% mean, and Tax Equity LTCG 13 0% mean? \nLiquid Fund Trades sheet, columns A, B, C, E, F are not following our proper formatting. Update them. \nIn the entire Excel file, except the trades sheet, everywhere the date is written, it is not following our formatting, background color, text color, and those kinds of formatting. Update the date column and date and time column. \nIn the rolling returns summary sheet, I cannot compare the strategy returns with the Nifty rolling returns properly. In this rolling returns summary, I want all of the rolling periods: 3 months, 6 months, 1 year, 2 years, 3 years, 5 years, 7 years, 7.5 years, and 10 years rolling return of the strategy and of the indices. And I want all the indices. \nCurrently, we have three sheets for rolling returns. I only want one sheet, as I mentioned above. \nAnd I want the exposure sheet correctly calculated and filled with the correct data. There is a column in the trades sheet called ENTRY_ATR_14. Remove that. Remove ATR 14 mention from all of the scripts, be it daily or weekly. In the trades sheet, the vwap_tight and the weekly_vwap_tight columns are not being filled. The entry_cumulative_rsi_2_2, entry_rsi_2, entry_intraday_intensity_21, weekly_intraday_intensity, mfi_10, and entry_daily_average_dollar_volume_200 all of these columns are not being filled correctly. Update the excel file to fill it correctly. And remove the columns from AQ to AT which contain the other indices, we do not need them. And move the entry_reason and exit_reason column after the candles_held column. And also move the stop_price column after the candle_held column. ",
