      "text": "Ran search for storyteller/salesman skills in Reel DB\nRan search specific storytelling and salesman skill notes\nRan scan for database + storytelling/salesman AI cognitive skills\nRan read storytelling & sales AI notes\nRan deep search storyteller and salesman AI skills in DB · Exited with code 1\nCreated find_story_sales.py\nRan run storyteller/salesman script\nCreated find_database_storytelling.py\nRan run database storytelling search\nCreated vault_wide_search.py \nRan run vault-wide search\n\nI have launched a focused vault-wide search across all notes in the database and AI Vault to pinpoint every exact skill, repository, prompt architecture, and MCP tool related to thinking like a storyteller or salesman. Analyzing the occurrences now.\n\nRan scan for think like / turn into expert prompt notes · Exited with code 1\nCreated find_think_like.py\nRan run find think like script\nRan clean up D:\\Temp Ai\n\nIn your database and across the analyzed notes, this exact problem is addressed: **giving an AI a raw database does not make it persuasive, narrative-driven, or conversion-focused.** Without a cognitive framework, an AI simply recites cold data points instead of knowing *how* to sequence emotion, handle resistance, and structure narrative arcs.\n\nThe exact **skills, GitHub repositories, MCP tools, and frameworks** identified in the notes that upgrade an AI to think like a storyteller and master salesman are detailed below:\n\n---\n\n### 1. The Core Repository: Turning Raw Knowledge Into Cognitive Skills\n* **`virgiliojr94/book-to-skill`** *(Featured in multiple notes, e.g. \"9 High-Value Open Source AI Repositories You Need\")*\n  * **What it does**: Rather than dumping entire PDFs, transcript databases, or reference books into the context window (which leads to context degradation and flat outputs), `book-to-skill` extracts the author's **mental models, psychological rules, behavioral frameworks, and persuasion mechanisms** into modular agent skills (`SKILL.md`).\n  * **Why it matters**: It provides the exact \"reasoning engine\" so the AI doesn't just read the database—it evaluates queries *through* the perspective of a master storyteller or veteran closer.\n\n---\n\n### 2. The Cognitive Storytelling & Narrative Intelligence Frameworks\nThe notes explicitly distinguish between \"summarizing facts\" vs. \"narrative intelligence\":\n* **Narrative Intelligence Framework** *(Note: `Mastering Narrative Intelligence to Make Your Ideas Stick`)*\n  * **Core Thesis**: Narrative intelligence is the ability to bridge the gap between dry data and human emotion. It instructs the AI never to present raw data; instead, it must filter facts through:\n    $$\\text{Person} \\longrightarrow \\text{Problem} \\longrightarrow \\text{Decision} \\longrightarrow \\text{Emotional Transformation / Outcome}$$\n* **A vs. B Script Analysis Skill** *(Note: `Turn Claude Into An Expert Scriptwriter With A vs B Analysis`)*\n  * **What it does**: A structured prompting engine where the AI is fed losing scripts vs. top-performing competitor scripts to extract retention hooks, pacing changes, tension curves, and punchline timing.\n* **The PAST Framework** *(Philipp Humm - `The Story Selling Method`)*\n  * **Architecture**: **Problem** $\\rightarrow$ **Agitate** $\\rightarrow$ **Story / Micro-moment** $\\rightarrow$ **Transformation**. Prevents the AI from preaching or reciting specs, forcing it to zoom into tangible sensory moments (location, actions, thoughts, dialogue).\n* **The CART Framework** *(Note: `Master Storytelling Using the CART Framework`)*\n  * **Formula**: Context, Action, Result, Takeaway. Used by the AI to convert boring case studies or statistical test results into gripping business narratives.\n* **The 100 Claude Scripting Prompts System** *(Note: `100 Claude Script Prompts That Hook Every Viewer`)*\n  * A dedicated 10-category prompting architecture for Claude (specifically Category `04 - Storytelling`) that overrides default corporate AI tone with audience-centric narrative perspectives.\n\n---\n\n### 3. The \"Think Like a Salesman\" & Persuasion Skill Architectures\n* **\"Think Like Alex Hormozi\" ($100M Money & Offer Engine)** *(Note: `Scale Your Business to $100M Using 7 Claude Prompts`)*\n  * **What it does**: A 7-prompt cognitive suite that forces the AI to look at raw product/service features and convert them into high-converting **Value Equations** ($(\\text{Dream Outcome} \\times \\text{Perceived Likelihood}) / (\\text{Time Delay} \\times \\text{Effort})$).\n* **The Straight Line & Tension De-escalation Skills** *(Notes: `10 Phrases to Lower Tension in Sales Conversations`, `The Salesman Who Tested 105,000 Phrases` - Elmer Wheeler)*\n  * **Rule**: \"Don't sell the steak, sell the sizzle.\" It teaches the model to eradicate needy phrases (\"Just checking in\", \"Does that make sense?\") and replace them with high-status, label/mirror sequences and outcome-first framing.\n* **Chase Hughes Behavioral Profiling Engine** *(Note: `Behavior Expert Chase Hughes on Covert Influence & Framing`)*\n  * Forces the AI to profile the user's micro-stress levels and defensiveness before suggesting an offer or asking for a commitment.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Relevant MCP Tools for Content & Persuasion Ingestion\n* **`Volume MCP`**:\n  * An MCP server that enables AI agents to ingest high-performing narrative carousels, decompose their psychological hook and slide-by-slide retention sequence, and repopulate them with tailored niche database insights.\n* **`Prompts.chat MCP`**:\n  * Connects an open repository of over 10,000 persona and role-based prompts directly into Claude Code / Cursor as an MCP server, allowing instant switching into designated sales copywriter and narrative dramatist personas.\n\n---\n\n### Summary: How the Database Directs You to Use Them\nIn your notes, the solution to make AI think like a storyteller/salesman is:\n1. **Never pass the raw database directly to the system prompt.**\n2. Use **`book-to-skill`** or modular persona rules (like your installed `deal-intelligence`, `sales-mastery-vault`, `hormozi`, and `chris-voss-negotiation` skills) as the **lens**.\n3. Have the AI retrieve the factual data from the database, but format the output strictly through the **Narrative Intelligence (Person $\\rightarrow$ Problem $\\rightarrow$ Decision $\\rightarrow$ Outcome)** or **PAST (Problem $\\rightarrow$ Agitate $\\rightarrow$ Story $\\rightarrow$ Transformation)** frameworks.",
      "fontSize": 1.1830985915492955,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Ran search for storyteller/salesman skills in Reel DB\nRan search specific storytelling and salesman skill notes\nRan scan for database + storytelling/salesman AI cognitive skills\nRan read storytelling & sales AI notes\nRan deep search storyteller and salesman AI skills in DB · Exited with code 1\nCreated find_story_sales.py\nRan run storyteller/salesman script\nCreated find_database_storytelling.py\nRan run database storytelling search\nCreated vault_wide_search.py \nRan run vault-wide search\n\nI have launched a focused vault-wide search across all notes in the database and AI Vault to pinpoint every exact skill, repository, prompt architecture, and MCP tool related to thinking like a storyteller or salesman. Analyzing the occurrences now.\n\nRan scan for think like / turn into expert prompt notes · Exited with code 1\nCreated find_think_like.py\nRan run find think like script\nRan clean up D:\\Temp Ai\n\nIn your database and across the analyzed notes, this exact problem is addressed: **giving an AI a raw database does not make it persuasive, narrative-driven, or conversion-focused.** Without a cognitive framework, an AI simply recites cold data points instead of knowing *how* to sequence emotion, handle resistance, and structure narrative arcs.\n\nThe exact **skills, GitHub repositories, MCP tools, and frameworks** identified in the notes that upgrade an AI to think like a storyteller and master salesman are detailed below:\n\n---\n\n### 1. The Core Repository: Turning Raw Knowledge Into Cognitive Skills\n* **`virgiliojr94/book-to-skill`** *(Featured in multiple notes, e.g. \"9 High-Value Open Source AI Repositories You Need\")*\n  * **What it does**: Rather than dumping entire PDFs, transcript databases, or reference books into the context window (which leads to context degradation and flat outputs), `book-to-skill` extracts the author's **mental models, psychological rules, behavioral frameworks, and persuasion mechanisms** into modular agent skills (`SKILL.md`).\n  * **Why it matters**: It provides the exact \"reasoning engine\" so the AI doesn't just read the database—it evaluates queries *through* the perspective of a master storyteller or veteran closer.\n\n---\n\n### 2. The Cognitive Storytelling & Narrative Intelligence Frameworks\nThe notes explicitly distinguish between \"summarizing facts\" vs. \"narrative intelligence\":\n* **Narrative Intelligence Framework** *(Note: `Mastering Narrative Intelligence to Make Your Ideas Stick`)*\n  * **Core Thesis**: Narrative intelligence is the ability to bridge the gap between dry data and human emotion. It instructs the AI never to present raw data; instead, it must filter facts through:\n    $$\\text{Person} \\longrightarrow \\text{Problem} \\longrightarrow \\text{Decision} \\longrightarrow \\text{Emotional Transformation / Outcome}$$\n* **A vs. B Script Analysis Skill** *(Note: `Turn Claude Into An Expert Scriptwriter With A vs B Analysis`)*\n  * **What it does**: A structured prompting engine where the AI is fed losing scripts vs. top-performing competitor scripts to extract retention hooks, pacing changes, tension curves, and punchline timing.\n* **The PAST Framework** *(Philipp Humm - `The Story Selling Method`)*\n  * **Architecture**: **Problem** $\\rightarrow$ **Agitate** $\\rightarrow$ **Story / Micro-moment** $\\rightarrow$ **Transformation**. Prevents the AI from preaching or reciting specs, forcing it to zoom into tangible sensory moments (location, actions, thoughts, dialogue).\n* **The CART Framework** *(Note: `Master Storytelling Using the CART Framework`)*\n  * **Formula**: Context, Action, Result, Takeaway. Used by the AI to convert boring case studies or statistical test results into gripping business narratives.\n* **The 100 Claude Scripting Prompts System** *(Note: `100 Claude Script Prompts That Hook Every Viewer`)*\n  * A dedicated 10-category prompting architecture for Claude (specifically Category `04 - Storytelling`) that overrides default corporate AI tone with audience-centric narrative perspectives.\n\n---\n\n### 3. The \"Think Like a Salesman\" & Persuasion Skill Architectures\n* **\"Think Like Alex Hormozi\" ($100M Money & Offer Engine)** *(Note: `Scale Your Business to $100M Using 7 Claude Prompts`)*\n  * **What it does**: A 7-prompt cognitive suite that forces the AI to look at raw product/service features and convert them into high-converting **Value Equations** ($(\\text{Dream Outcome} \\times \\text{Perceived Likelihood}) / (\\text{Time Delay} \\times \\text{Effort})$).\n* **The Straight Line & Tension De-escalation Skills** *(Notes: `10 Phrases to Lower Tension in Sales Conversations`, `The Salesman Who Tested 105,000 Phrases` - Elmer Wheeler)*\n  * **Rule**: \"Don't sell the steak, sell the sizzle.\" It teaches the model to eradicate needy phrases (\"Just checking in\", \"Does that make sense?\") and replace them with high-status, label/mirror sequences and outcome-first framing.\n* **Chase Hughes Behavioral Profiling Engine** *(Note: `Behavior Expert Chase Hughes on Covert Influence & Framing`)*\n  * Forces the AI to profile the user's micro-stress levels and defensiveness before suggesting an offer or asking for a commitment.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Relevant MCP Tools for Content & Persuasion Ingestion\n* **`Volume MCP`**:\n  * An MCP server that enables AI agents to ingest high-performing narrative carousels, decompose their psychological hook and slide-by-slide retention sequence, and repopulate them with tailored niche database insights.\n* **`Prompts.chat MCP`**:\n  * Connects an open repository of over 10,000 persona and role-based prompts directly into Claude Code / Cursor as an MCP server, allowing instant switching into designated sales copywriter and narrative dramatist personas.\n\n---\n\n### Summary: How the Database Directs You to Use Them\nIn your notes, the solution to make AI think like a storyteller/salesman is:\n1. **Never pass the raw database directly to the system prompt.**\n2. Use **`book-to-skill`** or modular persona rules (like your installed `deal-intelligence`, `sales-mastery-vault`, `hormozi`, and `chris-voss-negotiation` skills) as the **lens**.\n3. Have the AI retrieve the factual data from the database, but format the output strictly through the **Narrative Intelligence (Person $\\rightarrow$ Problem $\\rightarrow$ Decision $\\rightarrow$ Outcome)** or **PAST (Problem $\\rightarrow$ Agitate $\\rightarrow$ Story $\\rightarrow$ Transformation)** frameworks.",
